The files in this directory are copied from MAME 0.289 (https://github.com/mamedev/mame). They are
only built into development tools (the reference of Konami's boards, konami/reference/: kref and the
oracles), never into a game. The Z80 core the reference runs is the one in system32/reference/mame/z80/
(its own LICENSE); the YM2151 is ymfm's (konami/reference/ymfm/, its own LICENSE).

- src/devices/cpu/m68000/ (m68000/): the Motorola 68000 CPU core (m68000.cpp, m68000.h, m68kcommon.cpp,
  m68kcommon.h, and m68000.lst, from which m68000gen.py writes the core's steps at build time; copyright
  Olivier Galibert) and its disassembler (m68kdasm.cpp, m68kdasm.h; copyright Karl Stenerud).
  arcade-decomp's m68000/disassembler.py is a Python port of m68kdasm.cpp.
- src/devices/cpu/m6809/ (m6809/): the 6809 CPU core and Konami's CPU on it, the 052001 and 053248
  (m6809.cpp, m6809.h, m6809inl.h, konami.cpp, konami.h, and base6x09.lst, m6809.lst and konami.lst, from
  which m6809make.py writes the cores' steps at build time; copyright Nathan Woods, m6809make.py Olivier
  Galibert) and their disassembler (6x09dasm.cpp, 6x09dasm.h; copyright Nathan Woods, Sean Riddle, Tim
  Lindner). arcade-decomp's konami_cpu/disassembler.py is a Python port of 6x09dasm.cpp's
  konami_disassembler.
- src/mame/konami/ (konami/): the tile chip K052109 and the sprite chip K051960 (copyright Fabio
  Priuli, Acho A. Tang, R. Belmont), the sprite chips K053246/K053247 (k053246_k053247_k055673.cpp, .h)
  and konami_helper (copyright David Haywood), the priority encoder K053251 (copyright Fabio Priuli, Acho
  A. Tang, R. Belmont), konamipt.h (copyright Manuel Abadia), and the drivers tmnt.cpp (copyright Nicola
  Salmoria) and simpsons.cpp (copyright Ernesto Corvi).
- src/devices/sound/ (sound/): the K007232 (copyright Nicola Salmoria, Hiromitsu Shioya), the uPD7759
  (copyright Juergen Buchmueller, Mike Balfour, Howie Cohen, Olivier Galibert, Aaron Giles), the K053260
  (copyright Ernesto Corvi, Alex W. Jackson) and ymopm.cpp, .h, MAME's device for ymfm's YM2151
  (copyright Aaron Giles).
- src/devices/machine/eeprom.cpp, eeprom.h, eepromser.cpp and eepromser.h (machine/): the serial EEPROMs
  (the ER5911 among them); copyright Aaron Giles.
- src/emu/drawgfx.cpp, drawgfx.h, drawgfxt.ipp (copyright Nicola Salmoria, Aaron Giles), tilemap.cpp and
  tilemap.h (emu/), and src/lib/util/bitmap.cpp, bitmap.h, palette.cpp and palette.h (util/): the
  graphics MAME's video chips draw with; copyright Aaron Giles where not said.

The games' runtime/src/ (the board's memory map, its video and its sound chips) follow the behavior of these
files and of the drivers here under the same terms.

